# Git LFS is intentionally NOT used in this repository.
#
# ioc/threatbase-domain.txt and ioc/threatbase-hash.txt were tracked in LFS until
# 2026-08-16. Because they are regenerated in full on every feed run, each daily
# commit stored a complete new ~90 MiB / ~69 MiB blob (LFS never deltas), which
# exhausted the 10 GB LFS storage budget in about two months.
#
# Those two files are now git-ignored and published as GitHub Release assets on
# the rolling `latest` tag instead. Release assets are not billed against the LFS
# storage or bandwidth quotas. See .github/workflows/update-feed.yml.
#
# Do not add `filter=lfs` rules for any file that is rewritten on a schedule.
